@startuml
title SPDM TPM Integration

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #30343b
  LifeLineBorderColor #4a5160
  ParticipantBorderColor #555b66
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #eef1f7
  NoteBackgroundColor #fffde0
  NoteBorderColor #a6a06b
}

actor Requester
participant Responder
participant TPM
participant "TPM Identity Key" as Identity
participant "TPM IAK" as IAK

group Connection negotiation
Requester -> Responder: GET_VERSION
Responder --> Requester: VERSION
Requester -> Responder: GET_CAPABILITIES
Responder --> Requester: CAPABILITIES
Requester -> Responder: NEGOTIATE_ALGORITHMS
Responder --> Requester: ALGORITHMS
end

group Responder identity authentication
note over Requester, Responder
DIGESTS advertises both identity and IAK slots.
Both SlotIDs are retrieved with GET_CERTIFICATE
before CHALLENGE. The IAK SlotID (e.g. slot 1)
is reserved for Quote evidence verification and
must not sign SPDM transcripts. libspdm still runs
peer integrity/authority on GET_CERTIFICATE;
IAK env RootHash / OOB policy is applied at Quote.
end note
Requester -> Responder: GET_DIGESTS
Responder --> Requester: DIGESTS
Requester -> Responder: GET_CERTIFICATE (identity SlotID)
Responder -> TPM: TPM2_NV_Read(identity certificate)
TPM --> Responder: CertificateChainFragment
Responder --> Requester: CERTIFICATE

Requester -> Responder: GET_CERTIFICATE (IAK SlotID)
Responder -> TPM: TPM2_NV_Read(root cert;\nLIBSPDM_TPM_IAK_ROOT_CERT_INDEX)
TPM --> Responder: Root DER (for RootHash)
Responder -> TPM: TPM2_NV_Read(IAK certificate chain\nexcept root; sample: leaf only)
TPM --> Responder: CertificateChainFragment\n(IAK leaf [+ intermediate CAs])
Responder --> Requester: CERTIFICATE\n(spdm_cert_chain_t: RootHash +\nserved chain; sample: one leaf)
note left of Requester
Cache the full IAK CERTIFICATE
(spdm_cert_chain_t) for Quote-time trust
checks and leaf binding. libspdm peer
integrity/authority may run here; do not
apply LIBSPDM_TPM_IAK_* RootHash / OOB
policy until Quote verification.
end note

Requester -> Responder: CHALLENGE (identity SlotID)
Responder -> Identity: TPM2_Sign(Hash(transcript || nonce))
Identity --> Responder: SPDM signature
Responder --> Requester: CHALLENGE_AUTH
note over Identity
The TPM-backed responder identity key
continues to sign SPDM transcripts.
end note
end

group Signed GET_MEASUREMENTS with TPM Quote evidence
note over Requester, Responder
Quote opaque is generated and verified for
ALL_MEASUREMENTS (--meas_op ALL) and for each
signed single PCR hash index (--meas_op ONE_BY_ONE).
Non-PCR indices use the SPDM L1 signature only.
end note
Requester -> Responder: GET_MEASUREMENTS\n(ALL or PCR index, GenerateSignature,\nrequester nonce)
Responder -> TPM: TPM2_PCR_Read(selected PCR bank)
TPM --> Responder: PCR values
Responder -> IAK: TPM2_Quote(IAK, selected PCRs,\nrequester nonce)
IAK --> Responder: TPM2B_ATTEST + TPMT_SIGNATURE
note right of IAK
IAK is restricted to attestation.
It signs only TPM Quote evidence.
It never signs an SPDM transcript.
end note
Responder -> Identity: TPM2_Sign(SPDM transcript,\nidentity SlotID)
Identity --> Responder: SPDM signature
Responder --> Requester: MEASUREMENTS\n(record + SPDM signature + Quote opaque evidence)
note left of Requester
Verify independently:
* SPDM signature with identity certificate
* Quote nonce, PCR selection and PCR digest
* Cached IAK CERTIFICATE RootHash vs
  configured root (LIBSPDM_TPM_IAK_ROOT_CERT_FILE)
* Exclusive trust branch:
  - if LIBSPDM_TPM_IAK_CERT_CHAIN_FILE is set:
    verify that OOB chain to the configured
    root and require its leaf byte-match the
    SPDM slot leaf
  - else: verify the SPDM slot chain
    (root-excluded) to the configured root
* Quote signature with the IAK slot leaf
end note
note over Requester, Responder
Quote verification uses the cached IAK
CERTIFICATE for the slot selected by opaque
evidence; it does not re-issue GET_CERTIFICATE.
end note
end

group Requester authentication
Requester -> Responder: GET_ENCAPSULATED_REQUEST
Responder --> Requester: Encapsulated GET_DIGESTS / GET_CERTIFICATE / CHALLENGE
Requester -> Responder: DELIVER_ENCAPSULATED_RESPONSE
Responder --> Requester: Requester authenticated
end

group Existing TPM-backed KEY_EXCHANGE (unchanged)
Requester -> Responder: KEY_EXCHANGE
Responder -> Identity: TPM2_<KEY>_ZGen
Identity --> Responder: Shared secret
Responder -> Identity: TPM2_Sign(Hash(KEY_EXCHANGE_RSP transcript))
Identity --> Responder: SPDM signature
Responder --> Requester: KEY_EXCHANGE_RSP
note over Identity
KEY_EXCHANGE keeps using the existing
TPM-backed identity key path, not the IAK.
end note

Requester -> Responder: GET_ENCAPSULATED_REQUEST
Responder --> Requester: Encapsulated requester authentication
Requester -> Responder: DELIVER_ENCAPSULATED_RESPONSE
Responder --> Requester: Requester authenticated for session
Requester -> Responder: FINISH
Responder --> Requester: FINISH_RSP
end

group Secured session
Requester -> Responder: SECURED SPDM MESSAGE
Responder --> Requester: SECURED SPDM MESSAGE
Requester -> Responder: KEY_UPDATE
Responder --> Requester: KEY_UPDATE_ACK
Requester -> Responder: END_SESSION
Responder -> TPM: TPM2_FlushContext
TPM --> Responder: Session TPM objects flushed
Responder --> Requester: END_SESSION_ACK
end

@enduml
